waiver: harness-limit
reason: an aborting program is only observable as an exit code on the
  native backends. The wasm leg builds with PrintMainResult and recovers
  the exit code from a trailing stdout line, which a trapping program
  never reaches — the runner sees empty stdout and a trap, not 134. And
  docs/ARRAY-BOUNDS.md makes the ABORT normative on all four backends
  but deliberately not the code: the interpreter reports `array index N
  out of range [0, L)` and exits 1 so `fern -interp` stays readable. So
  the case asserts the one exit code two backends agree on, and the
  other two are covered by internal/e2e/array_bounds_test.go, which
  asserts non-zero-and-printed-nothing rather than a value.
